% =====================================================================
% Bibliography for "Whether, Not Which: Cross-Model Selective Prediction
% from One Cheap Prefill"
%
% Attribution rules enforced (see PRIOR_ART.md):
%   * RoR is cited as arXiv:2607.08665v1 for the formulation and the policy
%     we compare against; arXiv:2607.08665v3 is a substantially different
%     paper under a changed title and is cited separately for the
%     identification claim it now makes.
%   * The shadow-price/duality framing for LLM routing is Bouchard's.
%   * The Lagrangian relaxation, the randomised-mixtures theorem and the
%     convex-hull achievable set are Altman's; the reservation-value index
%     is Weitzman's.
%   * The goal of budgeted inference with a trained skip action is
%     ROI-Reasoning's; the rule max(0, max_m pR - c) is the textbook
%     Lagrangian dual and is claimed by neither.
%   * Encoder-target decoupling is the prefill-router paper's; we replicate.
%
% Entries marked "AUTHOR LIST TODO" are arXiv-era papers whose author lists
% are not recorded in the repo docs; verify against arXiv before submission.
% =====================================================================

